of custom VMs.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.710
Custom VMs is a great example.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.657
You don't really need to be
locked into any predefined VM.

00:05:19.657 --> 00:05:21.490
So think about if you're
running SQL Server.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:23.920
You don't need to run
it on a 16-core VM

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.014
when you just need 10 vCPUs.

00:05:26.014 --> 00:05:28.180
And that is really powerful,
especially for Windows,

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.490
