it working on-premise.

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:20.030
Yesterday we did a great
demonstration of this

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.370
and demonstrated failover.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.100
If you want to go
and see that talk,

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.180
please look at the recording
for running SQL Servers.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:29.930
But one thing I'd
really like to point out

00:09:29.930 --> 00:09:32.300
is we have detailed
guides and scripts.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.900
But setting up SQL HA
is not an easy process.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.844
Anyone who has set
up a SQL HA before?

00:09:37.844 --> 00:09:40.740
Oh, a few of you.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.600
So you know that this
is a multi-step process.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.115
A lot of things can go wrong.

00:09:45.115 --> 00:09:47.490
And just to get a proof of
concept takes a bunch of time.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.906
So what we've done is we've
got a Cloud Launcher template.

00:09:49.906 --> 00:09:54.520
In one click, you can set up
a multi-node cluster for you

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:55.370
in your project.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.370
And this is great if you
want to do a quick BOC,

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.862
you want to test
failover, just see

00:09:58.862 --> 00:10:00.070
how it works on the platform.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:04.580
So really I encourage you
to go and try that out.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.960
We talked about VSS.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.030
